"tabpanel" id="panel_r_0_0" aria-labelledby="tab_r_0_0"><div class="InfoBox-tabContainer-20hgy"><span class="ToggleExpandedCollapsed-wrapper-15z6N"><span class="ToggleExpandedCollapsed-area-tVFuj ToggleExpandedCollapsed-areaCollapsed-1_eQP" style="max-height: 120px;"><span class="rich-text-view"><p>Quarterly Conversations are integral to maintaining and driving high performance every quarter. They are an opportunity to reflect on your performance, plan for the next quarter, gain valuable feedback and discuss your career development.&nbsp;Find out more on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://version1.sharepoint.com/sites/Performance/SitePages/Quarterly-Conversations.aspx">Quarterly Conversations here</a>.</p><p><strong><u>Please Follow the Key Dates below</u></strong></p><p><strong>Employee Submission Deadline:</strong> Sunday 27th September, Employees complete and share their written&nbsp;self-assessments with their managers.</p><p><strong>Manager Submission Deadline</strong>: Sunday 11th October, Managers complete and share their written reviews with their direct reports.</p><p><strong>Alignment Period:</strong> Monday 12th - Thursday 15th October, All reviews and ratings will be reviewed by practice leads.</p><p><strong>Overall Ratings will be automatically released and shared: </strong>Friday 16th October, Everyone will receive a notification from Greenline, directing them to their Q3 review and their manager’s rating will be available, after which they can sign the review to complete the process.</p><p>To view objectives, feedback and previous Quarterly Conversations during this you can click the 'Helpful Resources' button at the top right of this page to view these whilst writing. Find more on this on the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://version1.sharepoint.com/sites/Performance/SitePages/Greenline.aspx">FAQ page</a>.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Please ensure that your written reviews remain high‑level and concise.</strong></p><p>Detailed discussions regarding performance, progress and development should be reserved for your Quarterly Conversation with your manager.</p></span></span><button aria-expanded="false" type="button" class="link-style ToggleExpandedCollapsed-toggle-2OJZv">Show more</button></span></div></div><div class="Tabs-tabPanel-K9sYC" role="tabpanel" id="panel_r_0_1" aria-labelledby="tab_r_0_1"></div></div></div><form novalidate="" class="ReviewEditForm-form-3qEW9"><div class="ReviewEditForm-section-1g__u"><div class="ReviewEditForm-sectionToWrite-178iA ReviewEditForm-sectionInner-37s8B"><h1>Reflection on Performance and Objectives for Next Quarter</h1><span class="rich-text-view"><p>When writing this section, use the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://version1.sharepoint.com/sites/Learning-and-Development/Shared%20Documents/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FLearning%2Dand%2DDevelopment%2FShared%20Documents%2FCPD%2FCPD%20Handbook%2Epdf&amp;parent=%2Fsites%2FLearning%2Dand%2DDevelopment%2FShared%20Documents%2FCPD">CPD handbook</a> to ensure your self‑reflection demonstrates the level of impact and behaviours expected for your role, including the competencies and expectations associated with your CPD Level and Stage.</p></span></div></div><div class="ReviewEditForm-section-1g__u"><div class="ReviewEditForm-sectionToWrite-178iA ReviewEditForm-sectionInner-37s8B"><label class="Heading-questionLarge-2GKST Heading-question-2kpVm" role="none"><div><span style="float: left; margin-right: 5px;">*</span><span class="rich-text-view"><p><strong>Reflection on Performance</strong></p><ul><li>Please demonstrate how you performed against your objectives as agreed at the start of the quarter?</li><li>Please demonstrate how you performed against the expectations for your <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://version1.sharepoint.com/sites/Learning-and-Development/SitePages/CPD-and-the-Promotion-Process.aspx#cpd-levels">CPD Level</a>?</li><li>